## cost summary (GET /api/cost/summary), repeated - review L-26 / M-19
  measured against src/api/queries.ts sha256:c4bf922499a7 (contains the string "token_usage_rollup": yes)
  that line is PROVENANCE, not a verdict: it pins these numbers to a source file so
  two runs are never compared without knowing whether they measured the same program.
  the request goes through the real route, so what is timed is whatever the query
  layer does today - this phase knows nothing about how the answer is produced.
  whichever read path that source implements, THIS phase measured THAT path. It is not a
  statement about the product until the source it names is the source the product ships.
  machine load, 1-minute average: 3.70 on 10 cores before these phases, 3.48 on 10 cores after.
  scale of the ledger this read covers:
    token_usage rows                                1324765
    distinct (session x model x day) groups             115   11519.7x fewer than rows
    distinct (session x model x bucket x day)           575   finest grain a rollup may use
    distinct sessions / models / days            53 / 3 / 7
  BOTH scales are printed because they decide different implementations: a read that
  scans the ledger pays the row count, a read backed by a persisted rollup pays the
  group count. Quoting one of them alone would misrepresent the other implementation.
  discipline: 1 warm-up iteration(s) discarded, 5 measured. Before EACH measured read one session grows by
  one record and one tick ingests it (both outside the timed span), so no read can be
  served as a repeat of the one before it.
